  eventID: WorkerRepeated
  dialogueLines:
  - 'The worker looks busy. Perhaps now isn''t the best time to interrupt him. '
  - He seems to have a lot on his plate. The player should probably leave him to
    it.
  - The worker is clearly in the middle of something. Best not to distract him.
  - He looks rather occupied. Perhaps the player should come back later.
  - Whatever he's doing, he seem to be taking it seriously. The player should leave
    him alone.
  - "The worker doesn\u2019t appear to have time for interruptions."
  - "He\u2019s busy working. Surely the player has somewhere else to be."
  - It seems this worker has enough to worry about without the player bothering him.
  - "The worker is concentrating. Interrupting him probably wouldn\u2019t be very
    helpful."
  - He appears to be quite busy. This might not be the right moment to talk to him.
  - The worker has work to do. The player should probably let him get on with it.
  - "He doesn\u2019t look like he\u2019s waiting for company."
  - The worker seems preoccupied. Perhaps it would be better to leave him alone.
  - Judging by his expression, he has more important things to worry about.
  - "He\u2019s clearly got his hands full. The player should probably move along."
  - Whatever has his attention, it seems rather important.
  - The worker appears to be deep in thought. Interrupting him might not be wise.
  - He seems rather engrossed in his work. Best to let him be.
  - This worker looks like he could use some peace and quiet.
  - "There\u2019s work to be done, and apparently, the player isn\u2019t part of
    it."
  canRepeat: 1
  priority: 3
